Subject: [PATCH] compose: a seed keeps its machine across Chrome updates

The composition root hashed the running Chromium build and catalogue
version with the seed, so every Chrome update or catalogue bump drew
almost every seed's hardware again: on 10,000 Windows seeds a patch
level build change gave 97% of them a different GPU. A persistent
profile presented a different device under the same cookies after an
upgrade.

Compose() now keys the root with frozen epochs, the values v0.4.2
hashed, so no existing seed moves and later builds draw the same
options. The composition still records and stamps the real build.
Bumping an epoch re-keys every seed, so it only happens on purpose.
Table edits still re-draw the axes they touch; recording the composed
machine in the profile directory is separate work.

diff --git a/base/apostate/compose.h b/base/apostate/compose.h
--- a/base/apostate/compose.h
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.h
@@ -124,10 +124,9 @@
 
 using Digest = std::array<uint8_t, 32>;
 
-// The tuple that keys the composition. Every field is part of the identity, so
-// changing any one of them is a different profile for the same seed -- which
-// is what makes a binary and a profile unable to silently disagree about what
-// the catalogue said.
+// The tuple that keys the composition. ComputeRoot hashes whatever it is given;
+// Compose() gives it the frozen epochs below for the three version fields, not
+// the running build's versions.
 struct BASE_EXPORT RootInputs {
   std::string_view profile_schema_version;
   std::string_view catalogue_version;
@@ -143,6 +142,17 @@
 //                 fingerprint_platform   0x00
 //                 seed )
 BASE_EXPORT Digest ComputeRoot(const RootInputs& inputs);
+
+// The version inputs Compose() hashes into every root. They are epochs, fixed
+// at the values v0.4.2 hashed, not the build's own versions: a persistent
+// profile keeps its machine (AGENTS.md), and hashing the running Chromium or
+// catalogue version made every Chrome update or catalogue bump re-draw nearly
+// every seed's hardware under the same cookies. The composition still records
+// and stamps the real versions. Bumping an epoch re-keys every seed, so it is
+// only ever done on purpose. scripts/profile_resolver.py mirrors these.
+inline constexpr std::string_view kRootSchemaEpoch = "3";
+inline constexpr std::string_view kRootCatalogueEpoch = "2";
+inline constexpr std::string_view kRootChromiumEpoch = "152.0.7977.83";
 
 // draw(label, i) = SHA-256( root 0x00 label 0x00 uint32_be(i) )
 //
diff --git a/base/apostate/compose.cc b/base/apostate/compose.cc
--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -969,9 +969,9 @@
   }
 
   const RootInputs root_inputs = {
-      .profile_schema_version = request.profile_schema_version,
-      .catalogue_version = request.catalogue_version,
-      .chromium_version = request.chromium_version,
+      .profile_schema_version = kRootSchemaEpoch,
+      .catalogue_version = kRootCatalogueEpoch,
+      .chromium_version = kRootChromiumEpoch,
       .fingerprint_platform = composition.platform,
       .seed = composition.seed,
   };
diff --git a/base/apostate/compose_unittest.cc b/base/apostate/compose_unittest.cc
--- a/base/apostate/compose_unittest.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose_unittest.cc
@@ -516,7 +516,32 @@
   EXPECT_NE(HexEncodeLower(first->root), HexEncodeLower(second->root));
   EXPECT_NE(ProfileJson(*first), ProfileJson(*second));
 }
+
+// A persistent profile keeps its machine across upgrades. A newer Chromium
+// build or catalogue version must not re-key the seed: the root, and so every
+// axis's pick, stays where the frozen epochs put it. Hashing the build's own
+// versions re-drew about 97% of machines on a patch-level Chrome update.
+TEST(ApostateComposeTest, AnUpgradeKeepsTheSeedsMachine) {
+  constexpr DispersionAxis kAxes[] = {kOsReleaseAxis, kCpuAxis, kFontAxis};
+  const HostCapability host = CapableHost();
 
+  const std::optional<Composition> before =
+      Compose(RequestFor("stable-seed", kAxes, host));
+  ComposeRequest upgraded = RequestFor("stable-seed", kAxes, host);
+  upgraded.chromium_version = "153.0.7990.0";
+  upgraded.catalogue_version = "3";
+  const std::optional<Composition> after = Compose(upgraded);
+
+  ASSERT_TRUE(before.has_value());
+  ASSERT_TRUE(after.has_value());
+  EXPECT_EQ(HexEncodeLower(before->root), HexEncodeLower(after->root));
+  EXPECT_EQ(ChosenId(*before, "anchor"), ChosenId(*after, "anchor"));
+  EXPECT_EQ(ChosenId(*before, "os_release"), ChosenId(*after, "os_release"));
+  EXPECT_EQ(ChosenId(*before, "cpu"), ChosenId(*after, "cpu"));
+  // The composition still reports the build it actually ran under.
+  EXPECT_EQ("153.0.7990.0", after->chromium_version);
+}
+
